                    was performed with test-time                                
                    augmentation (original + horizontal                         
                    flip), resulting in a strong AUROC                          
                    score of 0.9276, indicating good                            
                    classification performance on the                           
                    validation set. The model was saved                         
                    correctly for future inference.                             
                    Validation Metric: 0.9276                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose integrating MixUp                         
                    augmentation into the training loop                         
                    with an alpha of 0.4. During each                           
                    batch, we mix pairs of images and                           
                    labels using a sampled lambda, then                         
                    compute the loss as a weighted sum of                       
                    the BCE losses for both targets. This                       
                    atomic change can improve                                   
                    generalization without altering the                         
                    model architecture or validation                            
                    strategy. All other components                              
                    (augmentations, scheduler, TTA during                       
                    validation) remain the same to isolate                      
                    the effect of MixUp.                                        
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 5 epochs using                        
                    MixUp data augmentation and a                               
                    CosineAnnealingLR scheduler on a                            
                    DenseNet121 backbone pretrained on                          
                    ImageNet. Validation was performed with                     
                    test-time augmentation (horizontal flip                     
                    averaging), resulting in a strong AUROC                     
                    of 0.9150, indicating good                                  
                    classification performance on the skin                      
                    lesion malignancy task. The trained                         
                    model was saved and a prediction                            
                    function was implemented for inference                      
                    on new images.                                              
                    Validation Metric: 0.915                                    
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose replacing the                             
                    standard BCEWithLogitsLoss with a                           
                    binary focal loss (alpha=0.25, gamma=2)                     
                    to better focus the model on                                
                    hard‐to‐classify malignant examples and                     
                    mitigate class imbalance. This change                       
                    is isolated and does not affect the                         
                    data pipeline, model architecture,                          
                    optimizer, scheduler, or TTA                                
                    evaluation, allowing us to directly                         
                    assess the impact of focal loss on                          
                    validation AUROC.                                           
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors or                          
                    bugs. The model was trained using a                         
                    DenseNet121 architecture with FocalLoss                     
                    for 5 epochs, and validation was                            
                    performed with test-time augmentation                       
                    (horizontal flip). The achieved                             
                    validation AUROC of 0.9224 indicates                        
                    good performance on the malignant vs                        
                    benign classification task.                                 
