                    Design: I removed the extra `unsqueeze`                     
                    on mixup labels so that the target                          
                    shape `(batch, 1)` matches the output                       
                    shape, avoiding the `(batch, 1, 1)`                         
                    mismatch. The loss is now computed                          
                    directly with `labels_a` and                                
                    `labels_b`. Everything else remains                         
                    same, and we print the validation AUROC                     
                    at the end and save `submission.csv` in                     
                    `working/`.                                                 
                    Results: The training script ran                            
                    successfully without errors. The model                      
                    was trained for 5 epochs using mixup                        
                    augmentation and evaluated with                             
                    test-time augmentation (TTA) on the                         
                    validation set. The final validation                        
                    AUROC achieved was 0.8935, indicating                       
                    good performance in classifying                             
                    malignant versus benign skin lesions.                       
                    The script also includes a prediction                       
