                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I will replace the Adam                             
                    optimizer with AdamW including a small                      
                    weight decay and add a                                      
                    CosineAnnealingLR scheduler over the 5                      
                    epochs to gradually decrease the                            
                    learning rate, improving both                               
                    convergence and generalization. This                        
                    lightweight change doesn't affect the                       
                    data pipeline or model architecture and                     
                    often yields a higher AUROC with                            
                    minimal extra code. The weight decay of                     
                    1e-4 helps regularize the training. The                     
                    rest of the pipeline, including                             
                    augmentations and TTA for validation,                       
                    remains unchanged. The script prints                        
                    the final validation AUROC and saves                        
                    the trained model and a `predict()`                         
                    function for inference.                                     
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model was trained for 5 epochs using a                      
                    DenseNet121 backbone with                                   
                    CosineAnnealingLR scheduler. Validation                     
                    was performed with test-time                                
                    augmentation (original + horizontal                         
                    flip), resulting in a strong AUROC                          
                    score of 0.9276, indicating good                            
                    classification performance on the                           
                    validation set. The model was saved                         
