                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose replacing the                             
                    standard BCEWithLogitsLoss with a                           
                    binary focal loss (alpha=0.25, gamma=2)                     
                    to better focus the model on                                
                    hard‐to‐classify malignant examples and                     
                    mitigate class imbalance. This change                       
                    is isolated and does not affect the                         
                    data pipeline, model architecture,                          
                    optimizer, scheduler, or TTA                                
                    evaluation, allowing us to directly                         
                    assess the impact of focal loss on                          
                    validation AUROC.                                           
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors or                          
                    bugs. The model was trained using a                         
                    DenseNet121 architecture with FocalLoss                     
