                    Design: I propose adding ColorJitter                        
                    augmentation to the training pipeline                       
                    to increase robustness to color and                         
                    lighting variations, which can improve                      
                    generalization without changing model                       
                    architecture or training regime.                            
                    Specifically, we insert                                     
                    transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.2,                      
                    contrast=0.2, saturation=0.2, hue=0.1)                      
                    into the train_transform before                             
                    normalization and RandomErasing. All                        
                    other components—including DenseNet121,                     
                    AdamW+CosineAnnealingLR, RandomErasing,                     
                    and 10‐crop TTA—remain unchanged. We                        
                    retrain for 5 epochs and report the                         
                    validation AUROC.                                           
                    Results: The training and validation                        
                    processes completed successfully                            
                    without any errors. The model was                           
