                    with 10-crop test-time augmentation                         
                    (TTA), achieving a high AUROC of                            
                    0.9234, indicating strong model                             
                    performance in classifying malignant                        
                    versus benign lesions. The trained                          
                    model was saved correctly for later use                     
                    in prediction.                                              
                    Validation Metric: 0.9234                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose replacing the static                      
                    CosineAnnealingLR scheduler with a                          
                    dynamic OneCycleLR schedule that ramps                      
                    the learning rate up to a higher max                        
                    (e.g. 1e-3) then back down over the                         
                    course of training. This single change                      
                    often yields better convergence and                         
                    generalization with minimal code                            
                    modifications. We compute the total                         
                    training steps and step the scheduler                       
                    after every batch rather than each                          
                    epoch, leaving all other components                         
                    (model, augmentations, TTA, etc.)                           
                    unchanged.                                                  
                    Results: The code executed successfully                     
                    without errors. The training process                        
                    ran for 5 epochs using a DenseNet121                        
                    model with OneCycleLR scheduler and                         
                    data augmentations including 10-crop                        
                    TTA for validation. The model achieved                      
                    a validation AUROC of approximately                         
